.TH PARDUS-HEALTH-CHECK 1 "May 2026" "pardus-health-check 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pardus-health-check \- Modular security and system health check tool for Pardus GNU/Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pardus-health-check
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pardus-health-check
is a comprehensive security and system health evaluation tool for Pardus GNU/Linux systems.
It performs automated scans across four main modules, detects configuration issues, and
generates actionable diagnostic reports.

The tool evaluates system security on a scale of 0-100 and provides specific recommendations
for addressing identified issues.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging output for detailed diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cli
Output report as colored terminal text (default).
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-json FILE
Generate machine-readable JSON report and save to FILE.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-html FILE
Generate web-viewable HTML report and save to FILE.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Run all security checks (default behavior).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-packages
Check only APT package status and security updates.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-network
Check only open ports and network services.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-hardware
Check only hardware and connected devices.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-system
Check only system health (CPU, memory, disk, services).
.SH MODULES
.TP
.B APT Package Analysis
Detects outdated packages, missing security updates, deprecated software,
and broken dependencies. Analyzes package database against repository information.
.TP
.B Open Port Scanning
Identifies active network ports and running services. Categorizes ports by risk level
and identifies unexpected or dangerous open connections.
.TP
.B Hardware Inventory
Enumerates connected hardware, USB devices, kernel modules, and PCI devices.
Identifies unknown or unsigned components that may indicate configuration issues.
.TP
.B System Health Monitoring
Continuously monitors CPU usage, memory consumption, disk space, failed services,
and critical system logs. Generates unified health score with recommendations.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a complete system security check with colored output:
.B pardus-health-check --all
.TP
Generate a JSON report for integration with monitoring systems:
.B pardus-health-check --json /tmp/health-report.json
.TP
Create an HTML report for sharing with system administrators:
.B pardus-health-check --html ~/health-report.html
.TP
Check only package security status:
.B pardus-health-check --packages
.TP
Run with verbose logging for debugging:
.B pardus-health-check --all --verbose
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.TP
.B CLI (Colored Terminal)
Human-readable format with ANSI color codes showing:
- Overall security score (0-100)
- Breakdown by module
- Detailed findings with severity levels
- Actionable recommendations
.TP
.B JSON (Machine-Readable)
Structured data format suitable for:
- Integration with monitoring systems
- Automated processing and alerting
- Long-term trend analysis
- Script automation
.TP
.B HTML (Web-Viewable)
Styled HTML report for:
- Viewing in web browsers
- Sharing with stakeholders
- Generating reports for audits
- Professional presentation
.SH RISK LEVELS
Findings are categorized by severity:
.TP
.B CRITICAL (🚨)
Immediate action required. Security breach risk.
.TP
.B HIGH (⚠️)
Important issues affecting system security.
.TP
.B MEDIUM (⚡)
Configuration issues that should be addressed.
.TP
.B LOW (ℹ️)
Items to monitor and review.
.TP
.B INFO (ℹ️)
Informational findings for awareness.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /tmp/pardus-health-check.log
Default log file for all check results.
.TP
.B /var/log/pardus-health-check/
Optional persistent log directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All checks completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred during execution.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
Core utilities: apt, systemctl, ss/netstat, dpkg
.TP
Optional: dmidecode (for BIOS info), lsusb, lspci, lsblk
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR netstat (8),
.BR top (1)
